Dafny no longer assumes that a suspended co-recursive call has already established
its result's full type membership. The previous circular assumption could accept
a co-datatype with an impossible refined payload and allow clients to prove false.
Destructors, ordinary helper inputs, pattern bindings, and substituted defaults
now establish the existing type-membership obligations before introducing their
type facts. No axioms are added. The repair conservatively rejects some valid
destructive observations of productive self-calls that previously verified; see
[the compatibility explanation](../codatatype-refinement-boundaries.md).
